        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you run on a THERUN treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Only on the 20% Auto Incline model, which has a 55 by 20-inch belt and 12 mph. The other THERUN treadmills have belts of 43.3 to 47.2 inches and top out at 9 or 10 mph, which suits walking and light jogging. The walking pads are for walking.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the THERUN 400 lb treadmill really rated for 400 lb?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Treat it as unconfirmed. A TR04 listing claims 400 lb, but another TR04 listing with the same belt and the same 145 lb machine weight claims 300 lb, and a TR06 listing says 400 lb in its title and 300 lb in its bullets. Plan on 300 lb unless the seller confirms otherwise in writing.",
