      "therun walking pad",
      "is therun legit",
      "therun 20% incline treadmill",
      "therun incline treadmill",
      "therun treadmill warranty",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best THERUN Treadmill: THERUN 20% Auto Incline Treadmill", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Brand Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">THERUN Treadmill Reviews: Is THERUN Legit?</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        THERUN is a real Amazon brand, not a scam: on 21 November 2026 its treadmills and walking pads ran from about $80 to $800, most were sold and shipped by Amazon.com itself, and every listing we checked gave a one-year warranty. The catch is the listings, which sometimes contradict themselves on capacity, belt size and motor power. This guide sets out every current model and which figures to trust.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 21, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">Based on the brand’s published specifications and warranty terms, retailer listings and owner reports.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        Some links on this page are affiliate links: we may earn a commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
