        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>THERUN is legit: it is a real brand selling real machines on Amazon, most of them sold and shipped
            by Amazon.com, each listed with a one-year warranty. It is a budget brand, and its listings need reading
            with care, because several contradict themselves on capacity, belt size and motor power.</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Walking pads:</strong> about $80 to $115 on Amazon on 21 November 2026, 0.6 to 3.8, 6.2 or 7.6
            mph depending on the model, with one 5% incline pad.</li>
            <li><strong>Folding treadmills:</strong> about $194 to $450 for 43 to 47-inch belts, 9 to 10 mph and up to
            16% incline.</li>
            <li><strong>The runner:</strong> the 20% Auto Incline Treadmill, about $800, with a 55 by 20-inch belt and
            12 mph.</li>
            <li><strong>Warranty:</strong> one year on every THERUN listing checked (checked November 2026).</li>
            <li><strong>Seller:</strong> Amazon.com on most listings; THERUN US Direct, a third-party seller, on the
            flagship and one TR04.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The best-value THERUN for most people is the TR06 12% Auto Incline Treadmill at about $285, for incline
            walking and light jogging. The cheap 2-in-1 walking pad is a reasonable desk machine. The flagship is the
            only THERUN worth considering for running, and at $800 it has stronger competition. If you are weighing a
            similar budget brand, our review of the <a href="/wellfit-tm037-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Wellfit TM037</a> works through the same
            questions for another <a href="/best-walking-pads-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Amazon walking pad</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="is-therun-legit" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Is THERUN Legit, or a Scam?</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Nothing suggests THERUN is a scam.</strong> The machines exist, they are sold in volume on Amazon,
            and on most current listings the seller of record is Amazon.com itself, which means Amazon takes the order,
            ships it and handles the return. That is about as low-risk as buying from an unfamiliar brand gets. What
            THERUN is not is a brand with a long track record, a published spec sheet or an easy-to-reach support line,
            and that is where the doubts come from.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What points to a real, accountable product</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Amazon is the seller on most listings.</strong> Of the ten THERUN listings checked on 21 November
            2026, eight were sold by Amazon.com and two by THERUN US Direct, a third-party seller account.</li>
            <li><strong>Every listing gives a warranty.</strong> All ten list a one-year warranty in their product
            information, and one says “1 Year Manufacturer”.</li>
            <li><strong>It is a range, not a one-off.</strong> THERUN sells walking pads, budget folding treadmills and a
            $800 running treadmill, with model codes (YT05, TR04, TR06, NEW-TR07, T15 Series) that recur across
            listings. A brand that disappears after one product does not build a catalogue like that.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Why some buyers end up suspicious</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Listings that disagree with themselves.</strong> One TR06 listing says 400 lb in its title and
            300 lb in its bullets. The cheapest walking pad says 300 lb and a 40-inch belt in its title, then 265 lb and
            a 35.5 by 15-inch belt in its bullets. The details are in the comparison below.</li>
            <li><strong>The same model with different numbers.</strong> Two listings carry the TR04 model code and the
            same 145 lb machine weight, yet one claims 400 lb, 4.0 HP and 16% incline and the other 300 lb, 3.5 HP and
            15%.</li>
            <li><strong>No continuous motor ratings.</strong> Every THERUN listing gives a single horsepower figure, with
            no continuous rating. On budget machines that figure is usually a peak.</li>
            <li><strong>Thin support outside Amazon.</strong> An independent walking-pad comparison site, OCDevel,
            reports that THERUN sells through Amazon only, that its own website is a marketing page linking back to the
            listings, and that it found no direct support channel. We could not load a THERUN site to confirm either
            way.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            None of that is fraud. It is the normal state of an Amazon-first budget brand: the products are real, the
            marketing copy is loose, and the support runs mostly through Amazon. Buy on the lowest figure any listing
            gives, from a listing sold by Amazon.com where you can, and use the return window.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-therun" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Makes THERUN Treadmills, and Who Sells Them?</h2>
<p>
            We could not identify the company behind THERUN. The Amazon listings name the brand and, on two of them, a
            seller called THERUN US Direct, but none of the listing data we read names a manufacturer, a parent company
            or a country of origin, and we did not find an About page or company registration to cite. Like most
            Amazon-first fitness brands, THERUN almost certainly sources from contract manufacturers, which is why
            several of its machines share frames, belts and displays with near-identical models under other brand names.
            That is an inference from how the category works, not something THERUN states.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Sold by Amazon or by THERUN US Direct</h3>
          <p>
            The seller matters more than the brand on a <a href="/best-budget-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>budget treadmill</a>, because the seller decides how a return or a
            damaged delivery is handled. On 21 November 2026:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Sold by Amazon.com:</strong> the TR04 16% 400 lb listing, both TR06 12% listings, the Manual <a href="/best-incline-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Incline Treadmill</a>, and every walking pad checked.</li>
            <li><strong>Sold by THERUN US Direct:</strong> the 20% Auto Incline Treadmill and the TR04 15% 300 lb listing.
            The TR04 15% listing also showed a second THERUN US Direct offer at $529.99, about $106 more than the main
            price, so check which offer you are adding to your basket.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When Amazon.com is the seller, Amazon’s own return policy applies and Amazon deals with the delivery. When a
            third-party seller is named, read that seller’s return terms on the listing before buying, especially for a
            box that weighs well over 100 lb. Sellers can change at any time, so check the “Ships from” and “Sold by”
            lines on the day you order. Our guide to <a href="/best-treadmills-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">the best treadmills on Amazon</a> explains how marketplace sellers, fulfilment and returns fit together.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Model codes worth knowing</h3>
          <p>
            THERUN’s listing titles are long keyword strings rather than model names, so the model code in the product
            information is the most reliable way to tell machines apart. YT05 is the small flat walking pad. TR06 is the
            43.3-inch belt folding treadmill with 12% or 15% incline. NEW-TR07 is the manual incline version. TR04 is the
            larger 47.2-inch belt treadmill. The flagship appears as “T15 Series”. If you ask THERUN or Amazon about a
            machine, quote the ASIN and the model code, not the title.
          </p>
        </div>

