        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is THERUN a legit brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. THERUN sells real treadmills and walking pads on Amazon, most of them sold and shipped by Amazon.com, and every listing checked in November 2026 gave a one-year warranty. The weak points are listings that contradict themselves on capacity and belt size, and little support outside Amazon.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes THERUN treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The listings do not name a manufacturer, parent company or country of origin, and we could not find a company page to cite. Two listings are sold by a seller account called THERUN US Direct; the rest are sold by Amazon.com.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty do THERUN treadmills have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One year. Every THERUN listing checked on Amazon in November 2026 gave one year in its product information, and one said “1 Year Manufacturer”. None separated frame, motor and parts cover, so plan on one year for everything and keep your order confirmation.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which THERUN treadmill is best?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For most people, the TR06 12% Auto Incline Treadmill at about $285: powered incline to 12%, up to 9 mph and a 300 lb rating, sold by Amazon.com. For running, only the 20% Auto Incline Treadmill, at about $800, has a running-length 55-inch belt and 12 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you run on a THERUN treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Only on the 20% Auto Incline model, which has a 55 by 20-inch belt and 12 mph. The other THERUN treadmills have belts of 43.3 to 47.2 inches and top out at 9 or 10 mph, which suits walking and light jogging. The walking pads are for walking.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the THERUN 400 lb treadmill really rated for 400 lb?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Treat it as unconfirmed. A TR04 listing claims 400 lb, but another TR04 listing with the same belt and the same 145 lb machine weight claims 300 lb, and a TR06 listing says 400 lb in its title and 300 lb in its bullets. Plan on 300 lb unless the seller confirms otherwise in writing.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where can I buy THERUN treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Mainly on Amazon. An independent comparison site reports that THERUN sells through Amazon only and that its website links back to the Amazon listings. Buy from a listing sold by Amazon.com where you can, so Amazon’s return policy applies.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

